#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:5
#: b49d9589363342628810dba411054005
msgid "Using SITL with Morse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:10
#: 595ea784af024e0eb68db08a09bdc0d8
msgid "`Morse <http://www.openrobots.org/morse/doc/stable/morse.html>`__ is an open robotics platform that uses python APIs and the blender 3D environment to create a complete robotics platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:14
#: 2bf114918b36462eb431b5bb49ec25b4
msgid "ArduPilot has a Morse SITL simulation backend that allows ArduPilot to control vehicles created within Morse."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:19
#: b4738d3e48df49359e3f51656e5adcce
msgid "Morse is no longer maintained so we recommend developers use :ref:`AirSim <sitl-with-airsim>` or :ref:`Webots <sitl-with-webots>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:23
#: c4bb43642bb44fe6b7fbc2e390fc4dee
msgid "Morse has only been tested on Linux/Ubuntu environments"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:26
#: 7d03681b95ba4f4f8a30ea7141e56cd4
msgid "Installing Morse"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:28
#: f32b9a00a1ff4445b0eafb90da35f122
msgid "`Official instructions can be found on openrobots.com <http://www.openrobots.org/morse/doc/stable/user/installation.html>`__. Morse uses the Blender Game Engine API to render the build scripts. If the user is installing Morse on Ubuntu 20.04 or later, install the software from the source(manual installation) as described on the Morse installation page(mentioned above). But for older Ubuntu  installs all you need is"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:35
#: 51535b72284947a89051703595b8e6b2
msgid "Checking the blender version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:36
#: e126ef1a4bb34cbcb563235a0f27fda9
msgid "As mentioned above, Morse relies on the Blender Game Engine for rendering the simulations. Given the fact that the newer Blender versions (**v2.80** and above) have discontinued the support for the game engine, users are requested to ensure that the installed `Blender version <https://download.blender.org/release/>`__ ranges between **v2.65**  to **v2.73** (Official version limit stated by Morse)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:40
#: 4ba1ac04b74744ebbc002953d6f14880
msgid "Blender **v2.74** - **v2.79** are also valid versions, as these versions also provide access to a stable Blender Game Engine. The below image shows ArduPilot's quadcopter Morse simulation running with Blender 2.76."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:47
#: 77053915b3fe498ba91ccfd2b5b1b060
msgid "Builder Scripts"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:49
#: 53487c301dea4d6faa47c2f9466c2104
msgid "The Morse simulator has the concept of builder scripts, which are python scripts setup to run within the Morse/Blender environment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/sitl-with-morse.rst:52
#: 73176e75a21d4722b2c4495004b87058
msgid "Some example builder scripts for use with ArduPilot are provided in the `ArduPilot/libraries/SITL/examples/Morse directory <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries/SITL/examples/Morse>`__."
msgstr ""

